@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-pleiotropy-closure> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "An edit to a gene must be shown changing every node the map links that gene to (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "A decidable check that every node a gene is linked to in a genotype map is among the nodes an edit to that gene is shown to change; its truth implies the inclusion, and one missing node makes it false. It bounds what a picture of an edit may leave out, and says nothing about how much any node changes." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Favored.lean) as an extension of the neutral case of Kimura (1962) to non-opposing selection; no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "closureB mapped changed = true  =>  forall n in mapped, n in changed" ;
    skos:definition """theorem closure_of_check {mapped changed : List String} (h : closureB mapped changed = true) :
    ∀ n ∈ mapped, n ∈ changed"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Genotype.closureB" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Genotype.closure_of_check", "Delphi.Genotype.closure_violated" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "A statement about pictures, not about development: it bounds what a view may omit, never how much a node changes. The map records links (expressed in, required for, sufficient for), so a node no source studied is unstudied, not gene-free, and the closure is only as complete as the sources." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Genotype.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-pleiotropy-closure> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-pleiotropy-closure> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-genotype-pleiotropy-closure> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-genotype-pleiotropy-closure> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Genotype.closure_of_check with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 23.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Genotype.lean (224 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Genotype.closure_of_check, Delphi.Genotype.closure_violated: Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:58:20.213Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [pleiotropy-closure-reversed] Statement changed to claim the closure check is TRUE when a mapped node is missing from the changed list, which is exactly when it is false. Rejected with 1 error(s): Genotype.lean:174:49: error: Application type mismatch: The argument Controls: 16 of 16 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-pleiotropy-closure> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

